.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH iface 1  "iface " 
.SH NAME
iface \- Interface table: name, mac, ipv4s, mtu, up
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBiface\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-iface\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-v \fR]... [\fB\-\-no\-autofill\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fINAME\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Interface table: name, mac, ipv4s, mtu, up
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-iface\fR \fI<IFACE>\fR
Interface for send/recv
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format: raw|hex|text|json|jsonl
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Verbosity (repeatable: \-v info, \-vv debug, \-vvv trace)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-autofill\fR
Disable every autofill/derivation (unspecified numeric fields → 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Validate the crafted packet after encode (violations → exit 2)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fINAME\fR]
Show a single interface by name
